# mutgap2_rdec_use_heaps_count_placement: Commands that look objects up, checked before they do, in a service task with a placement list (opcode 68) whose entries start zero: an object nothing has made yet (none is listed in the exec) is made by its first lookup and writes its placement entry (a heap or buffer its GPU address; an argument-buffer sampler its resourceIndex and ID). 0x86 UseHeaps, 0x1b UseHeapsWithStages, 0x87 UseResources and 0x89 UseResourcesWithStages with count 2 and one ref: the size check throws "Too many resources specified" before any lookup, so each exec faults and its object's entry stays zero. 0x8e SetFragmentSamplerState at index 16 (maxVertexSamplers) raises "Invalid sampler index" before its lookup: the entry stays zero; at index 0 the sampler is looked up (its entry written) and the exec faults at the setter (docs/testing.md 6.16: this encoder has no lodBias setter). Last, an exec that lists heap 1 and names it in 0x86 makes it. Isolate only: placement entries are written only in the service. host: the written values are the host's.
